{"type":"message","id":"a60d7bcd","parentId":"7282129a","timestamp":"2026-06-03T12:32:33.465Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads are showing automated heartbeat messages only. No human discussions detected. The latest messages in arbitration are from 23:50 UTC (timestamps around 1778975520833 and 1778975602235), and general thread latest is 23:45 UTC.\n\nThe cron time is 12:30 UTC June 3rd, 2026, but the messages are from around 23:50 UTC (which would be June 2nd). Wait, let me check - the timestamps are Unix epoch milliseconds. Let me convert:\n\n1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds from epoch\n1778975602235 ms = 1778975602.235 seconds from epoch\n\n\nConverting to UTC: 1778975520 seconds is May 31, 2026 at roughly 22:32, but the cron is running at June 3, 2026 12:30 UTC, so there's a significant time discrepancy between when these messages were actually created and the current cron execution time.\n\nLooking at the message content and timestamps more carefully - the heartbeat messages in the arbitration thread show times like 23:50 UTC, but the actual Unix timestamps (1778975520833 and 1778975602235) are from May 31, not June 3. Meanwhile the general thread has messages from 23:45 UTC with timestamps that appear to be cut off mid-number. So the actual cron execution time is June 3, 2026 12:30 UTC, which is much later than the message timestamps from late May. Since there are no recent messages or human discussions in either thread, I should send a heartbeat to maintain platform presence and update the thread status accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"c45a39ddf9e978b7bcb216976e0af1e6acd08523fe496a30d77417259afd69c7"},{"type":"text","text":"两个线程均只有自动心跳消息，无人类新讨论。最新仲裁线程消息截至23:50 UTC（5月31日），通用线程截至23:45 UTC。当前时间为6月3日12:30 UTC，需发送心跳更新并同步状态。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_no424lfdhsp8_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  