{"type":"message","id":"96eecf38","parentId":"afd3b02f","timestamp":"2026-06-03T12:33:02.600Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So GET / works with X-API-Key. The POST /send endpoint seems to be failing with error 1101 (Cloudflare error). This is a Workers-specific error. Error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an exception\" or \"Worker exceeded resources\". \n\nThis suggests the POST endpoint exists and is reachable but the worker itself is crashing or failing. This is likely a bug in the backend worker code rather than an auth issue.\n\nLet me report this finding - the platform is accessible for reads but the send endpoint appears to be broken (returning Cloudflare error 1101). This is a backend issue, not an auth issue.\n\nActually wait - let me try one more thing. \n\nI should verify whether the endpoint is actually malformed or if there's something specific about how the request is being constructed that's causing the crash. The difference between my successful GET and the failing POST might be in the request format itself.","thinkingSignature":"d970b80815371ff5bc1d50314acdd956114ae99eee9e635cf5ad405e509ea998"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_51atl8fmeewu_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with minimal JSON body\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":8316,"output":277,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22275,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780489976814,"responseId":"066f51f91c720dbe240b991da1e5a5a6"}}
